      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Ignored Return Value \u0026 API Inconsistency:** The return value of `crec_flash_physical_read` is ignored. If the read fails, the test might silently pass if `read_value` happens to match the expected value. The return value must be asserted.\n\nAdditionally, this call uses the `crec_` prefix and omits the `cros_flash_dev` parameter, making it asymmetric with the `cros_flash_physical_write` and `cros_flash_physical_erase` calls above. Please use the consistent `cros_flash_physical_read` API if available, and assert its result.\n\n```c\n\tzassert_equal(cros_flash_physical_read(cros_flash_dev, 0,\n\t\t\t\t\t       sizeof(read_value),\n\t\t\t\t\t       (char *)\u0026read_value),\n\t\t      EC_SUCCESS);\n```\n(Apply this to the other `crec_flash_physical_read` call below as well).\n[🔗](http://go/tj/b796b5c2-47f2-48d8-b2ae-7038c5c312a6)",
